{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792495366,"nonce":"rgKTOgL0rHRrBdf1x0jyQMS0ED0=","message":"Design settled 2026-10-20, with the plan at `~/.claude/plans/gb-19-release-enable-it-goofy-biscuit.md`. **This branch does the binary release only.** Enable web app release, and the others, stay here as later branches.\n\n\nThree keys, no environments:\n\n```toml\n[release]\nbinaries = [\"./cmd/git-board\"]\nplatforms = [\"linux/amd64\", \"linux/arm64\", \"darwin/amd64\", \"darwin/arm64\", \"windows/amd64\"]\nbuild = \"make dist\"   # optional\n```\n\nA table with binaries and no environments is enabled. The existing rules then give what a binary release wants: every cut is a final (no candidate environment), deployed nowhere (no last environment). An artifact kind per entry (GB-18) is deferred: these keys are what a binary entry would say, so they move there later without a rewrite.\n\n\nIn a clean detached checkout of the tag (the `checkout` the deploys use, so `git describe` reports the tag). Built-in: `CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags \"-s -w\"` per platform, a `.tar.gz` (`.zip` for windows) holding `\u003cbinary\u003e_\u003ctag\u003e_\u003cos\u003e_\u003carch\u003e/` with the binary, LICENSE and README.md, and `checksums.txt` (sha256). With `build` set, that command runs instead and whatever it leaves in `dist/` ships: git-board needs this for its embedded web bundle.\n\n\nAfter the tag is pushed: `gh release create \u003ctag\u003e --verify-tag --notes-file …  dist/*`, the notes being the draft's (the issues merged since the previous final), the same as the record's. GitHub only for now, inferred from the remote's URL; a gitlab or gitea remote gets a clear \"not yet\" at Enable time. `gh` joins the install hints. This overrides the PRD's non-goal \"no GitHub Releases mirroring\" for binaries: a binary release *is* a GitHub release.\n\n\nThe release record gains `assets`: the archives' names and sha256. The release's page lists them under Archives, from git, without asking GitHub.\n\n\nWith no `[release]` table, the Releases page shows what it found (`cmd/*/main.go`, a Makefile `dist` target, the remote and its forge, the default platforms), the TOML it will write, and **Enable binary release**. The server infers (`GET /api/releases/setup`), writes the table textually like `[github-project]` is written, keeping the file's comments (`POST /api/releases/setup`), and runs it at once. No field editing in the panel: edit `.git-board.toml` for anything else.\n\nLive checks go to guilbep/git-board-test only. git-board's own `.git-board.toml` gets the inferred block on this branch, so the next git-board release is cut from its Releases page.","files":null}]}